e in the heat of the moment that are hard to keep later","Not enough attention to details and deadlines","A tendency to talk more than listen"],"motivation":["Recognition and approval","Communication and teamwork","Freedom of self-expression","Novelty and variety of tasks"],"stress":"Under pressure you become scattered and impulsive, avoid unpleasant conversations and may see the situation as rosier than it is. Open discussion and support from colleagues help.","communication":["A personal connection first, the agenda second","Room to speak up and talk ideas through","Public recognition of your contributions","A written recap of what was agreed — it helps both sides"],"environment":"An open, friendly environment with plenty of contact, recognition and freedom from rigid procedures. Isolation and monotony drain your energy."},"S":{"traits":["Patient","Reliable","Calm","Attentive to people","Consistent"],"strengths":["You can be relied on over the long haul","You know how to listen to and support others","You work patiently and methodically","You bring the team together and defuse conflicts"],"growth":["Resistance to change, even beneficial change","Difficulty saying no and standing your ground","Keeping disagreement to yourself to preserve the peace"],"motivation":["Stability and predictability","Sincere appreciation for your contribution","Clear expectations and ground rules","Working in a close-knit team"],"stress":"Under pressure you withdraw, become overly accommodating and put off decisions. Sudden change and open conflict are especially hard to bear. Time to adjust and a calm conversation help.","communication":["Advance notice of changes and an explanation of why they’re needed","Being asked for your opinion directly — you rarely volunteer it","No pressure, and time to answer without being rushed","Appreciation for your specific contributions"],"environment":"A stable environment with clear processes, good relationships and a reasonable pace of change. Chaos, 